course: dictionary
lesson: 5857
title: Meet the mamba
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mamba is a fast, very venomous snake from Africa. Venomous means it has venom, a poison it can inject through a bite. There are black mambas and green mambas. You can learn a lot about a word from the sentences around it.
explain: Read this sentence: «Black mambas are grey or olive-brown; the name comes from the inky black inside of the mouth.» The clue is the word name. The writer is telling you that the snake's name does not come from its skin, which is grey or olive-brown. It comes from the black inside of its mouth.
explain: Some sentences warn you about myths, or false ideas. «Snake charmers' cobras do not dance to music, mambas do not chase horses, and sucking out venom does not help a bitten friend.» The words do not are the clue. Each one corrects something people wrongly believe.
explain: Mambas are dangerous, so never approach or touch a wild snake. If you see one, move away slowly.
fact: A mamba is a fast, very venomous snake from Africa.
fact: There are black mambas and green mambas.
fact: The black mamba is one of the fastest snakes on land.
fact: The black mamba's name comes from the inky black inside of its mouth, not its skin, which is grey or olive-brown.
fact: Never approach or touch a wild snake; move away slowly.
exercise: «Black mambas are grey or olive-brown; the name comes from the inky black inside of the mouth.» Why is the black mamba called black? | Because its skin is jet black all over | Because it only comes out at night | Because it hides in dark caves | *Because of the inky black inside of its mouth
exercise: A mamba is a fast, very venomous snake. What does venomous mean? | Fast as a racing car | Covered in hard, shiny shell | *Full of poison that it can inject through a bite | Able to fly very high
exercise: «Snake charmers' cobras do not dance to music, mambas do not chase horses.» What do the words do not tell you? | *The sentence is correcting a common myth | The snakes are really dancing | Snake charmers are always right | Mambas love chasing horses
test: Which snake is one of the fastest on land? | Cobra | *Black mamba | Rattlesnake | Viper
test: Where does the mamba come from? | Australia | Asia | South America | *Africa
exam: What should you do if you see a wild snake? | Pick it up to look closer | Throw a stone at it to scare it | Chase it slowly to see where it goes | *Move away slowly without touching it
